  "working": "Identify product containing named element for each reaction and determine hybridization d²sp³ (octahedral low-spin). (i) Zn in cyanide process likely forms Zn(CN)2 or Zn complex; Zn2+ is d10, not d²sp³. (ii) S in H2S2O7 dilution gives H2SO4 etc, S in sulfate (S6+?) sulfate ion is tetrahedral? Not d²sp³. (iii) Co with NH3 excess gives Co(III) complex possibly low-spin Co(NH3)6^3+ which is d²sp³? Co3+ d5 low-spin gives t2g5, uses d²sp³? Actually octahedral low-spin uses d²sp³ (t2g + eg? low-spin uses t2g and d orbitals? Typically d²sp³ for octahedral complexes with strong field leads to low-spin using dxy,dxz,dyz (t2g) and dz2,dx2-y2 (eg) plus s,p? Hybridization d²sp³ includes two d, one s, three p. So Co(III) low-spin could be d²sp³. However reaction includes air bubbled through, may oxidize Co to Co(II) or Co(III) hydroxide. Likely Co(OH)3 precipitate, not d²sp³. (iv) C from Al4C3 + HCl gives CH4, carbon not hybridized. (v) Cu2+ with KCN excess forms [Cu(CN)4]2- maybe square planar? Cu(II) often d9, not d²sp³. (vi) Cr3+ with NaOH gives Cr(OH)3 precipitate, not d²sp³. (vii) CuCl2 with excess Cl- forms [CuCl4]2- tetrahedral or square planar, not d²sp³. (viii) Ag with KCN and O2 gives AgCN or Ag(CN)2-? Silver cyanide AgCN is linear? Not d²sp³. Thus none have d²sp³ hybridized product. Count = 0.",
